1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,700
What makes Black people being involved in local government so important?

2
00:00:02,880 --> 00:00:05,000
Because local government is where the rubber meets the road.

3
00:00:05,180 --> 00:00:11,680
No one is going to ask their state representative, their congressman, even the president, like for anything.

4
00:00:11,840 --> 00:00:14,900
They're going to ask their local council person, older person, mayor.

5
00:00:15,040 --> 00:00:19,400
And that's where everything hits when you think about basic functions, right?

6
00:00:19,480 --> 00:00:24,700
If people's trash can't get picked up, if they can't get their kids to school, if there's no after-school program,

7
00:00:24,920 --> 00:00:29,240
if they don't have access to public transportation, if they don't have internet, all of these things,

8
00:00:29,240 --> 00:00:33,520
most of which are not the responsibility of local government, but that's what they're going to bring to the table

9
00:00:33,520 --> 00:00:35,620
if they don't feel safe in their communities.

10
00:00:35,800 --> 00:00:38,100
And we have to be focused in local government.

11
00:00:38,400 --> 00:00:42,760
And what we have to do as Black people is, one, realize the importance of local government,

12
00:00:42,900 --> 00:00:48,840
but also the importance of understanding where all other levels of government flow into that

13
00:00:48,840 --> 00:00:50,260
and who to hold responsible.

